> I did run against master and the project works fine in all ways. You've rebased against master as well, so only these changes are likely involved. I wouldn't have reported the issue against this PR otherwise. :)

Yes, but quite a few of the errors were caused from something else in the project already failing to compile and the PR being unable to handle the failure case silently. While we shouldn't have regressions in behavior like that and the engine should keep working under those conditions, I did handle most of them already by the virtue of just not crashing with an assert.

But I can't fix the shader compilation errors on the project itself and those are most likely not related to the PR. It'd be best for content to not rely on errors behaving the same between major changes, as it's not exactly guaranteed we'll handle all those errors silently in the future. By compilation errors I mean stuff like:
